<p>Whether you&rsquo;re a new user or a seasoned pro, ScreenCastsONLINE offers in-depth screencasts on a wide range of topics, from tutorials to app discovery. <a href="https://screencastsonline.com/members/aff/go/bterpstra">Check it out.</a></p>

<dl>
  <dt><a href="https://david-alves.com/practical/">Practical</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Practical sits on top of Calendar and Reminders on your Mac: your next meeting counts down in the menu bar, ⌘J joins the call, its docs open on your iPhone too, and a missed reminder stays on today until it&rsquo;s done. €40 once. Your calendar never leaves your Mac.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>The niftiest feature is being able to type something about a reminder, say, &ldquo;push 2 hours&rdquo;, and have it adjust for you. Plus, drop in a screenshot of a ticker or invite and have the event fill in automaticall.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://riffcalendar.com/">Riff Calendar</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Riff is an iPhone calendar you navigate by zooming. The same calendar goes from half a year to your day, hour by hour. And it is as direct as paper: hold a free slot, type the title, done.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>Hat tip to Dan Peterson</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://muglobe.com/">MuGlobe</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Discover music by place. Explore genres, artists and musical traditions on MuGlobe’s interactive world map, listen to recordings and read their stories.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>This is so cool. Drag the globe around to pinpoint a region and get a playlist of current music for that area, with &ldquo;more info&rdquo; that breaks down the common genres and styles for that region. Check the &ldquo;? Help&rdquo; button for all the tricks.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://shotbolt.app/">Shotbolt</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>Shotbolt is a screenshot and screen recording app for Mac. Change any arrow or note after you save, and find any screenshot by a word in it. Free, no account.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>There&rsquo;s a $9.99 (sale price) one-time purchase to unlock Pro. The coolest feature that sets it apart is its ability to OCR tables and convert them to TSV. That&rsquo;s always been a sticking point for screen capture OCR apps for me.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>

